module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.Trivialized
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GoodOpenClose.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistEpi.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.FinitelyGenerated

/-!
# Tag 01N1's third assertion, reduced to invertibility of one pullback

Let `ψ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ` be a homomorphism of nonnegatively graded rings, surjective on homogeneous
components of all sufficiently large degree, and suppose `𝒜` is generated in degree one over
`𝒜 0`. Tag 01N1's third assertion is that Tag 01MY's comparison map `θ n` on every twist is an
isomorphism. This file proves it from a single remaining input — invertibility of the *source*
of `θ n` — and proves everything else the assertion needs.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.isIso_projMapData_twistMap_of_isInvertible_source`:
  **the reduction.** Under the tagged statement's two hypotheses `hψ` and `hgen`, and the extra
  hypothesis that `(mapHom)^* 𝒪_{Proj 𝒜}(n)` is invertible, the comparison map on the `n`-th
  twist of Tag 01MY's bundle is an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.isInvertible_target`: the *target* of the comparison
  map, `ι^* 𝒪_{Proj ℬ}(n)`, is invertible.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.mapDomain_le_ratioLocus_one`: the domain of definition
  `U(ψ)` lies in the degree-one ratio locus of `ℬ`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.ratioLocus_eq_top_of_adjoin_coe_degree_one` and
  `span_coe_degree_one_eq_irrelevant`: the statement's generation hypothesis, at the two spellings
  the existing lemmas want.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.range_coe_degree_one`: the coercion bridge between the
  statement's generating set `(𝒜 1 : Set A)` and the existing lemma's
  `Set.range fun f : 𝒜 1 => (f : A)`.

## The route

Epimorphy of `θ n` is proved for all `n` with no generation hypothesis, as Tag 01N0's twist
assertion. An epimorphism between invertible sheaves of modules on a scheme is an isomorphism,
which is the companion file. So the assertion needs exactly invertibility of the two sides of
`θ n`, both sheaves on the open subscheme `U(ψ)` of `Proj ℬ`.

The target is `ι^* 𝒪_{Proj ℬ}(n)` for the open immersion `ι : U(ψ) ⟶ Proj ℬ`, and that is the
shape the Tag 01MU result produces: the twists `𝒪(dn)` become invertible after
restriction to any open contained in the degree-`d` ratio locus. Here `d = 1`, so what is needed
is `U(ψ) ≤ ratioLocus ℬ 1`, and generation in degree one gives it. A point of `U(ψ)` omits
`ψ f` for some homogeneous `f` of positive degree; generation in degree one makes the irrelevant
ideal of `𝒜` the ideal generated by `𝒜 1` (Tag 07Z4), so if the point's prime contained `ψ g`
for every `g` of degree one it would contain `ψ f`; hence the point omits some `ψ g` with
`g ∈ 𝒜 1`, and `ψ g` has degree one, so the point lies in `D₊(ψ g)` with `1 ∣ 1`.

## What is not done

**The source is not shown to be invertible, and the reduction below is therefore not the route
by which Tag 01N1's third assertion is proved.** Its hypothesis `hsrc`, invertibility of
`(Scheme.Modules.pullback (ProjTwistCompare.projMapData 𝒜 ℬ ψ).hom).obj (twistingSheaf 𝒜 n)`,
is discharged neither here nor anywhere. The twist is invertible upstairs —
`ratioLocus 𝒜 1 = ⊤` by `ratioLocus_eq_top_of_adjoin_coe_degree_one`, which is proved here and
used by nothing else in this file — but transporting invertibility along the pullback of the
*closed* immersion `mapHom : U(ψ) ⟶ Proj 𝒜` would need invertibility to be local on the base,
and `Stacks.InvertibleLocallyFree.InvertibleIsLocal` is undischarged.

The assertion itself **is** proved, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjTwistMono/Assembly.lean`, as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.isIso_projMapData_twistMap`, under exactly the statement's
three hypotheses and without `hsrc`. That route replaces invertibility by an isomorphism with
the unit on each member of a cover and globalizes with `isIso_of_isIso_restrict_locally`: being
an isomorphism is a proposition and *is* local on the base, which invertibility is not known to
be. The reduction below is kept because it is true and short, and because `isInvertible_target`
— the invertibility of the *target*, which does come from Tag 01MU — is used by nothing else.

Tag 01C8 does *not* help with `hsrc`, although it is the same mathematics: the root-namespace
`pullback_isLocallyFree` of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/LocallyFreePullback.lean` proves that the pullback
of a locally free sheaf of modules along a morphism of ringed spaces is locally free with the same
index set. What it concludes is local freeness, in the `RS.Modules` vocabulary of sheaves of
modules on an `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace`, whereas `hsrc` asks for
`SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` of a `Scheme.Modules` pullback; no lemma identifies the two, and
supplying one is not done here.

Nothing here attaches a Tag 01N1 label, and the reduction is *not* the statement of Tag 01N1: it
carries one hypothesis that statement does not.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry HomogeneousIdeal TopologicalSpace CategoryTheory Opposite
open Filter
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono

universe u w w'

variable {A B : Type u} {σ : Type w} {τ : Type w'}
  [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]

/-! ### The generation hypothesis of the statement -/

omit [CommRing A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A] [GradedRing 𝒜] in
/-- The two spellings of "generated in degree one over the degree-zero part": the statement writes
the generating set as the coercion of `𝒜 1`, the existing lemma as the range of the inclusion of
`𝒜 1`. They are the same set. -/
theorem range_coe_degree_one : (Set.range fun f : 𝒜 1 => (f : A)) = (𝒜 1 : Set A) :=
  Subtype.range_coe

/-- **The ratio locus is everything when the source is generated in degree one**, at the
spelling of the generating set that Tag 01N1's third assertion uses. -/
theorem ratioLocus_eq_top_of_adjoin_coe_degree_one
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set A) = ⊤) (d : ℕ) :
    ProjShared.ratioLocus 𝒜 d = ⊤ :=
  ProjShared.ratioLocus_eq_top_of_adjoin_degree_one 𝒜
    (by rwa [range_coe_degree_one]) d

/-- Generation in degree one makes the irrelevant ideal the ideal generated by `𝒜 1`. -/
theorem span_coe_degree_one_eq_irrelevant
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set A) = ⊤) :
    Ideal.span (𝒜 1 : Set A) = (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒜).toIdeal := by
  rw [← range_coe_degree_one 𝒜] at hgen ⊢
  exact (generates_algebra_iff_generates_irrelevant 𝒜 (fun f : 𝒜 1 => (f : A))
    (fun _ => 1) (fun _ => Nat.one_pos) (fun f => f.2)).mp hgen

/-! ### The domain of definition lies in the degree-one ratio locus -/

/-- **The domain of definition lies in the target's degree-one ratio locus.** A point of the
domain omits `ψ f` for some homogeneous `f` of positive degree; generation in degree one writes
`f` in the ideal generated by `𝒜 1`, so the point already omits `ψ g` for some `g` of degree
one, and `ψ g` has degree one. -/
theorem mapDomain_le_ratioLocus_one (ψ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ)
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set A) = ⊤) :
    ProjShared.mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ ψ ≤ ProjShared.ratioLocus ℬ 1 := by
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨d, f, hd, hf, hfy⟩ := (ProjShared.mem_mapDomain_iff 𝒜 ℬ ψ y).mp hy
  by_contra hcon
  refine hfy ?_
  have hsub : (𝒜 1 : Set A) ⊆ (Ideal.comap (ψ : A →+* B)
      y.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal : Set A) := by
    intro g hg
    by_contra hgmem
    exact hcon (ProjShared.basicOpen_le_ratioLocus ℬ (dvd_refl 1) (Graded.map_mem ψ hg) hgmem)
  have hspan : (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒜).toIdeal ≤
      Ideal.comap (ψ : A →+* B) y.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal :=
    (span_coe_degree_one_eq_irrelevant 𝒜 hgen) ▸ Ideal.span_le.mpr hsub
  exact hspan (HomogeneousIdeal.mem_irrelevant_of_mem 𝒜 hd hf)

/-! ### Invertibility of the target of the comparison map -/

/-- **The target of Tag 01MY's comparison map on twists is invertible** once the source ring is
generated in degree one: the domain of definition lies in the target's degree-one ratio locus,
and the twists are invertible after restriction to any open of the ratio locus. -/
theorem isInvertible_target (ψ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ)
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set A) = ⊤) (n : ℤ) :
    SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (ProjShared.mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ ψ).toScheme.presheaf
      (ProjShared.mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ ψ).toScheme.ringCatSheaf.2
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (ProjShared.mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ ψ).ι).obj
        (twistingSheaf ℬ n)) := by
  have h1 : ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ) * n = n := by rw [Nat.cast_one, one_mul]
  exact h1 ▸ GoodOpenClose.isInvertible_pullback_twistingSheaf_of_le_ratioLocus ℬ
    (mapDomain_le_ratioLocus_one 𝒜 ℬ ψ hgen) n

/-! ### Tag 01N1 part (3), reduced to invertibility of the source -/

/-- **Tag 01N1's third assertion, reduced to one input.** If the pullback of the `n`-th twist
along the induced morphism is invertible, then Tag 01MY's comparison map on the `n`-th twist is
an isomorphism, under exactly the two hypotheses of the statement.

The three other ingredients are discharged here: the comparison map is an epimorphism by Tag
01N0, its target is invertible by `isInvertible_target`, and an epimorphism between invertible
sheaves of modules on a scheme is an isomorphism by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono.isIso_of_epi_of_isInvertible`. No bridge is needed on
the conclusion: the bundle's twist map is the standalone comparison map by definition, and the
epimorphism result is stated on the same term. -/
theorem isIso_projMapData_twistMap_of_isInvertible_source (ψ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ)
    (hψ : ∀ᶠ d : ℕ in atTop, Function.Surjective (GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom ψ d))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set A) = ⊤) (n : ℤ)
    (hsrc : SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (ProjShared.mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ ψ).toScheme.presheaf
      (ProjShared.mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ ψ).toScheme.ringCatSheaf.2
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (ProjTwistCompare.projMapData 𝒜 ℬ ψ).hom).obj
        (twistingSheaf 𝒜 n))) :
    IsIso ((ProjTwistCompare.projMapData 𝒜 ℬ ψ).twistMap n) := by
  have := hsrc
  have := isInvertible_target 𝒜 ℬ ψ hgen n
  exact isIso_of_epi_of_isInvertible _
    (ProjTwistEpi.epi_projMapData_twistMap_of_eventually_surjective 𝒜 ℬ ψ hψ n)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistMono

end
